        "thinking": "`pino-http` destructures `{ pino, symbols: { stringifySym, chindingsSym } }` from the pino module. Our shim doesn't export `symbols`. I need to add those to the pino shim.\n\nWhat are `stringifySym` and `chindingsSym`? These are internal pino symbols:\n- `stringifySym` - a Symbol used as a property key for JSON stringify function\n- `chindingsSym` - a Symbol used as a property key for child bindings\n\nFor our stub, we can just export placeholder symbols. The `pino-http` package uses these to look up internal pino state. \n\nI need to export a `symbols` object from our pino shim with these two symbols so `pino-http` can destructure them without crashing, even though they won't actually do anything meaningful since we're not using real pino.\n\nBut wait—I should check if `pino-http` is even necessary in a Cloudflare Worker environment, since it might not be compatible or needed at all.",
